Third-party notices for web/vendor/tdweb/
=========================================

tdweb.js and the *.worker.js chunks are webpack bundles: they inline several
MIT-licensed dependencies whose individual notices the bundler stripped. Those
declared by the upstream tdweb package.json are listed here so the attribution
survives redistribution.

  TDLib (tdweb)        Boost Software License 1.0   see ./LICENSE
  regenerator-runtime  MIT   Copyright (c) Facebook, Inc. and its affiliates
  @babel/runtime       MIT   Copyright (c) 2014-present Sebastian McKenzie and contributors
  localforage          Apache-2.0  Copyright (c) 2013-2017 Mozilla
  uuid                 MIT   Copyright (c) 2010-2020 Robert Kieffer and other contributors
  broadcast-channel    MIT   Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Meyer

The .wasm is machine-executable object code, which BSL-1.0 exempts from the
notice-reproduction requirement; tdweb.js and the worker chunks are distributed
in source form and are not exempt, which is why this file exists.

Provenance of this build (TDLib commit, toolchain) is recorded in
web/tdweb-build/. Rebuild with the Dockerfile there rather than trusting these
bytes.
